{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And the rabble that was in its midst craved a craving</b> etc. until 'and Moshe gathered.' All of this was in three days — on the twentieth of Iyyar, and the twenty-first of it, and the twenty-second of it." "<b>VeHa'asafsuf.</b> Written with alef, and not read (with alef, i.e. the vocalization lacks the consonantal alef)." "<b>[That was in its midst</b> — and they were not in the middle of the camp]. <b>And they sat and wept — also the children of Israel.</b> After the rabble had already complained on their own, they turned back and complained together with the rabble, and wept over the craving for meat." "<b>Who will feed us meat.</b> For the manna had ceased from the first order. This verse teaches us that they complained about the eating of meat."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {1 "The comment notes that the word אספסף is written plene with a consonantal alef that is not reflected in the received vocalization.", 3 "'משנה ראשונה' likely refers to the earlier arrangement of manna, implying the manna supply had by then lapsed."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:17:23.759410247Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}